msgid "Bootstrapping the project"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"First, you need a new project that contains the OpenShift extension.\n"
"Then, before you build and deploy your application, you must log into an "
"OpenShift cluster."
msgstr ""

msgid "Adding the OpenShift extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To build and deploy your applications as a container image that runs inside "
"your {openshift} cluster, you must add the {project-name} OpenShift "
"extension `quarkus-openshift` as a dependency to your project."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This extension also generates {openshift} resources such as image streams, "
"build configuration, deployment, and service definitions.\n"
"If your application includes the `quarkus-smallrye-health` extension, "
"{openshift} can access the health endpoint and verify the startup, liveness, "
"and readiness of your application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"From {project-name} 3.8, the `DeploymentConfig` object, deprecated in "
"OpenShift, is also deprecated in {project-name}.\n"
"`Deployment` is the default and preferred deployment kind for the `quarkus-"
"openshift` extension.\n"
"If you redeploy applications that you deployed before by using "
"`DeploymentConfig`, by default, those applications use `Deployment` but do "
"not remove the previous `DeploymentConfig`.\n"
"This leads to a deployment of both new and old applications, so, you must "
"remove the old `DeploymentConfig` manually.\n"
"However, if you want to continue to use `DeploymentConfig`, it is still "
"possible to do so by explicitly setting `quarkus.openshift.deployment-kind` "
"to `DeploymentConfig`."
msgstr ""

